    {
      "id": "n2",
      "type": "note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "label": "About this template",
      "s": {
        "text": "After a base load flow this takes out each line and transformer in service in turn (the base case first), runs the load flow and reads the loading of every line and 2-winding transformer and the voltage of every busbar (three reads side by side: they run one after another, then the row is added). Each outage gets a row, also one that does not converge (with its reason); the worst outage is printed at the end. Fill in the project."
      },
      "pin": [],
      "sv": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "type": "pf.ldf",
      "x": 320,
      "y": 0,
      "label": "Base load flow",
      "s": {
        "net": "case",
        "qlim": "case",
        "taps": "case"
      },
      "pin": [],
      "sv": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n5",
      "type": "pf.cont.foreach",
      "x": 640,
      "y": 0,
